#115 says records found only in a paper's text are listed after those found in a title or abstract. neurostuff/neurostore#1884 does not guarantee that. With `search_full_text=true` it runs one BM25 query over the title (boost 3), the abstract (2) and the paper's preferred full text (0.5), and each word may match in any of them, so a paper whose text matches strongly can outrank a weak title or abstract match.

This rewords two descriptions.

`search_full_text` now says:
- only the preferred full text is searched, the copy `fulltext_id` names;
- each word may match the title, the abstract or that text;
- a quoted phrase must sit within one of them;
- text-only matches usually rank lower, but that order is not guaranteed.

The shared `search` parameter now says:
- words are matched whole after English stemming, not as substrings or prefixes;
- words are AND-ed unless joined by OR;
- quoted phrases, AND, NOT, a leading `-` and parentheses are understood;
- a search of digits only matches the PMID.

The old text, "search for entries that contain the substring", was never true of the tsvector search either.

Nothing else changes. This goes with neurostuff/neurostore#1884, whose spec submodule points at this branch (`af474b0`).

