## Intent

Read DERIBIT_VENUE_START_ERROR.md and apply the Deribit venue startup fix without mistakes, then create a pull request. Prevent current Deribit currency catalogues such as AAVE from crashing product hydration; fetch the public instrument catalogue independently of wallet currencies, preserve typed API/HTTP/parsing failures, reject malformed or unsupported records observably, and keep supported product metadata accurate. Limit the initial supported scope to BTC/ETH inverse futures and perpetuals; explicitly reject options, spot, combo, and linear contracts until their semantics are safely modeled. Keep the change limited to public market-data/product hydration: no live requests in tests, no credentials, no order submission, no execution changes, and no change to send_orders safety. Use deterministic offline behavioral tests and query-aware cassettes.

## What Changed

- Fetch the public all-currency instrument catalogue independently of wallet currencies and preserve typed API, HTTP, and parsing errors.
- Validate catalogue records and hydrate only supported BTC/ETH inverse futures and perpetuals, logging malformed or unsupported instruments.
- Add deterministic offline coverage and query-aware fixtures, and document the supported Deribit product scope.

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: The change is bounded to Deribit response handling and product hydration, preserves typed failures, filters unsupported catalogue records observably, and the latest fixes correctly enforce query scope and canonical expiry metadata without introducing a substantiated new defect.

## Testing

Ran the focused Deribit tests, then started real Tai venue processes against an isolated local HTTP server serving mixed, unsupported, API-error, HTTP-error, and malformed responses. Direct catalogue querying, product metadata, observable rejection, and typed failure propagation all passed; no UI surface required visual evidence.

- Live validation: ✅ go - 6 of 6 scenarios driven live against the product

| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Starting a Deribit venue with a mixed current catalogue hydrates only accurate BTC/ETH inverse products | ✅ pass | live | Live Tai venue startup transcript shows a successful venue start with BTC perpetual expiry nil and ETH dated-future expiry at 2026-12-25 08:00 UTC, while malformed AAVE and unsupported option, linear,… |
| Product startup fetches the public instrument catalogue independently of wallet currencies | ✅ pass | live | Disposable Deribit server request log records only `/api/v2/public/get_instruments?expired=false&amp;currency=any` requests and no currency-catalogue endpoint. |
| A catalogue containing no supported products fails startup explicitly and observably | ✅ pass | live | Live transcript shows warnings for malformed, option, linear, and combo instruments followed by `[products: :no_supported_instruments]` and a VenueStartError. |
| A Deribit JSON-RPC API error reaches venue startup unchanged | ✅ pass | live | Live transcript shows `[products: {:api_error, %{&#34;code&#34; =&gt; 10001, &#34;message&#34; =&gt; &#34;invalid_params&#34;}}]`. |
| A Deribit HTTP failure reaches venue startup with status and body intact | ✅ pass | live | Live transcript shows `[products: {:http_error, 503, &#34;catalogue unavailable&#34;}]`. |
| Malformed successful HTTP content becomes a typed parsing failure rather than a crash | ✅ pass | live | Live transcript shows `[products: :invalid_json]` and a VenueStartError. |

