RFC 0001 row F4. OpenCode moves from the production Rust const to the data-only `plugins/agents/opencode/agent.toml`, compiled by the registry build. This follows F1 (#127, codex) and F2 (#134, claude-code). No behaviour or byte changes.

## Changes
- `crates/agent/src/catalog.rs`:
  - removes `OPENCODE`, its `Described` adapter and the `opencode_dir` / `opencode_json` / `opencode_jsonc` path functions;
  - `catalog()` fills the `opencode` slot from the compiled list. After merging main (#149, #131), a built-in id missing from the compiled list is a hard `AgentError` ("built-in agent `opencode` has no compiled description"); the frozen const is a fallback only under `legacy-agent-consts`, like codex and claude-code;
  - static `adapters()` is now `[_; 1]` (gemini-cli);
  - `Slot::V1` and `Slot::OpenCodeModels` and their engine arms are compiled only under `cfg(any(test, feature = "legacy-agent-consts"))`.
- `crates/agent/src/legacy.rs`: the const and its path functions move here unchanged (byte-identical to main b1e6739). Adds `#[doc(hidden)] pub fn opencode()`. `compiled.rs` and `rewrite.rs` tests use it.
- `RESERVED_AGENT_IDS` = `["gemini-cli"]`, plus a fixture-collision test for the shipped `opencode` id.
- `plugins/agents/opencode/agent.toml`: two JSON candidates on all three OSes, both with `env_override = "XDG_CONFIG_HOME"` and `env_replaces = "~/.config"`:
  - first `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` with `create = false`;
  - then `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` with `create = true`.

  The sets are `provider.hofund.name` (literal `hofund`), `npm` (literal `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`), `options.baseURL` (v1), `options.apiKey` (token) and `models` (catalog_models). The model key is `model`.
- CLI: `connect_models_note(adapter_id, model_count)` keeps the OpenCode models note after the adapter becomes compiled. A test covers 0 and 2 models, and None for codex, claude-code and gemini-cli.
- Goldens: `fixtures/all/` has 12 cases: fresh, existing-json-user, existing-jsonc, both-files (jsonc edited, json untouched), existing-stale-hofund, single-route, several-routes, no-routes, configured-model, xdg-absolute, xdg-relative (with a decoy), xdg-empty.
  - `shipped_agents_match_their_golden_cases` replays them through the compiled plugin.
  - `legacy_opencode_replays_compiled_goldens_for_every_target_os` replays them through the frozen const on Linux, macOS and Windows.
- `plugins/registry/tests/opencode_equivalence.rs` compares the compiled plugin with the frozen const on every target OS. Its `tree()` compares directories as well as files. It covers:
  - description fields;
  - the full lifecycle;
  - invalid JSON;
  - broken-file disconnect;
  - read and revert;
  - detect with only a config file and with only a binary;
  - disconnect removes the empty directory it created, and keeps one that holds a user file;
  - non-UTF-8, BOM and CRLF input.
- `crates/agent/src/lib.rs`: Windows mixed-case `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` test.
- Daemon/catalog tests: `find("opencode")` is None statically, and the catalog resolves it from the compiled list. Registry `tests/agents.rs` expects 3 compiled agents.
- Docs: CHANGELOG, RFC "PR F4 notes" (and the test-only slot list now includes `V1`), architecture, feature-parity 5.1, coverage/agents.md.

## Verification
- `cargo test --workspace --all-features`: 642 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored. Default features give the same result. This PR adds 14 tests.
- These all exit 0:
  - fmt;
  - clippy `-D warnings`, default and all-features;
  - rustdoc `-D warnings`;
  - `check-plugins`;
  - `workspace_invariants`;
  - `git diff --check`.
- Mutation checks: each mutation was applied to a copy, then the copy was restored. All 25 behavioural mutations failed tests or the build:
  - the apiKey key;
  - jsonc `create = true`, json `create = false`;
  - swapped candidate order;
  - renamed or removed `env_override`;
  - the Linux, macOS and Windows json paths, and the Windows jsonc path;
  - a Windows AppData path, rejected by build validation;
  - models to literal;
  - baseURL v1 to origin;
  - npm literal;
  - model key;
  - removing the name set or `[model]`;
  - the oracle's default directory, and the oracle ignoring XDG;
  - the engine skipping empty-directory removal;
  - the catalog not skipping opencode;
  - the CLI note off;
  - opencode still reserved, rejected by build validation;
  - deleted fixtures;
  - one flipped golden byte;
  - jsonc dropped from both-files;
  - a stray golden file.

  A stray **empty directory** in a golden `after/` is not caught. The kit checker only compares files (#148), and git cannot store empty directories.

## Parity notes (vs the upstream reference @ cbbf316, `internal/agent/agents.go`)
Matches:
- jsonc is preferred over json when both exist (`openCodeLike` :760-768);
- `opencode.json` is the file created by default;
- the directory is `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opencode`, else `~/.config/opencode` on every OS, and an empty XDG means unset (`homes` :79-86);
- a relative `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is treated as unset, as hofund's #114 rule does: upstream reads it through `appdir.Getenv`, which reports a non-rooted path variable as unset (`internal/appdir/env.go` :64-79, :84-92, :101-113);
- stale provider keys are kept, `models` is replaced wholesale and stale routes are dropped (`openCodeKept` :460-490);
- baseURL is the gateway plus `/v1` (:363-389).

Not in F4 scope (F4 must stay byte-identical to the pre-F4 const), so these are follow-up candidates:
- `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` (:926-938);
- the legacy `config.json` fallback (:763-768);
- per-model `modalities`, `limit`, `reasoning` and `variants`, and keeping user-added variants (:363-389, `openCodeVariants` :613);
- `small_model` (:781, :822);
- removing the provider when the model is unset and nothing still uses it (:784-801);
- configured-model spelling: upstream recognizes `<provider>/<model>` for its own gateway provider (:186-205), while `warn_unrouted_model` compares the raw string, so `hofund/route-a` warns "has no route";
- reusing a user provider that already points at the gateway (:849-889);
- Check/Sync semantics: Check verifies baseURL and apiKey only when the model is on the gateway (:805-811), Sync restores a removed provider block (:812-818) and rewrites on key-order drift (`internal/agent/sync.go` :185-197);
- the `oc` alias, User-Agent attribution and `auth.json` own-provider model options (:287, :773, :903-906).

The WSL twin, OpenChamber coupling and the mimocode/deveco forks are tracked as their own rows in `docs/coverage/agents.md`.

Upstream has no equivalent of the CLI models note.

